		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=43959#p43959"><![CDATA[
Bullet does not integrate kinematic objects forward.  Instead it relies on custom external logic (e.g. stuff the game dev wrote) to supply their world transforms every substep.  Typically this is done by supplying a <strong class="text-strong">MotionState</strong> that does the Right Thing inside its <strong class="text-strong">getWorldTransform()</strong> override.<br><br>Usually kinematic objects follow a scripted non-physical motion.  Think: moving platforms or other gamey mechanics that don't need to be reactive to collisions from other objects.  It would be challenging (and questionable) to try to make a kinematic object that tries to move dynamically.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=11033">drleviathan</a> — Mon Mar 28, 2022 4:53 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
